1.cssSelector
========================
What is Css?
------------------
Css is cascaded style sheet its language use to provide styles to webelements


What is cssSelector?
-----------------------------
-cssSelector It is locator to identify WebElement based on Css Property(css id,classname,attribute)
-CssSelector can travel in one direction(parent tag to child tag)
-CssSelector is faster than xpath

Syntax:
-----------------
1.tagname with id
2.tagname with attribute
3.tagname with className
4.tagname with id,className,attribute


1.tagname with id
---------------------------
Syntax:
--------------
tagname#id

example:
----------------
<input id="email-id">

input#email-id OR #email-id


2.tagname with attribute
--------------------------------
Syntax:
--------------
tagname[attribute='value']

Example
----------------
<input placeholder="Password" type="password">

input[type='password']
OR
input[placeholder='Password']


3.tagname with className
-----------------------------
Syntax:
-----------
tagname.className

Example: 
----------
<button class="btn btn-default btn-primary">
				c1     c2          c3	

button.btn.btn-default.btn-primary

OR

button.btn


4.tagname with id,className,attribute
--------------------------------------
Syntax:
--------------
tagname#id.className[attribute='value']

Example:
------------
<button id="submit-id" type="submit" class="btn btn-default btn-primary" </button>

button#submit-id.btn[type='submit']

==============================================================
CssSelector with Special symbols
-----------------------------------------
CssSelector does not provide any method support but cssSelector have symbols
that we use to uniquly identify elements

1.*(contains())
--------------------------
Based on partial element value match we can identify element

Syntax:
===============
tagname[attribute*='partial value']

<input id="twotabsearchtextbox">

input[id*="searchtext"]......1 of 1

2.^(starts-with())
------------------------------
Based on prefix value match we can identify element
Syntax:
===============
tagname[attribute^='prefix value']

<input id="twotabsearchtextbox">

input[id^="twotab"]......1 of 1


3.$(ends-with())
-------------------------
Based on suffix value match we can identify element
Syntax:
===============
tagname[attribute$='suffixvalue']

<input id="twotabsearchtextbox">

input[id$="box"]......1 of 1

