By xpath
=============
what is Xpath?
------------------
- xpath is path of element from its html or xml code
- xpath identify element directly from DOM (Document object model)
- Xpath can travel from parent to child and viceversa
- Xpath support multiple methods
- Xpath support axies(relations in between node)

Html DOM
-------------------
<html>---------------root node
<head>
</head>

<body>
<div>
<a>
<input>------------element
<button>

</body>
</html>
====================================
Types Of Xpath
====================
1.Absolute Xpath
---------------------
- It identify element from its root node
- It always starts with '/'

/html/body/div[2]/div/div/div/div[2]/div/form/div[1]/input

2.Relative xpath
---------------------
- It identify webelement based on its relative property
- It always starts with '//'

//*[@id="input-email"]

here * indicate all(from all the tags identify element whose id is input-email)

Syntax
==========
//tagname[@attribute='value']


Xpath With Operators
============================
1. and
-------------
Syntax:
-----------
//tagname[@attribute1='value' and @attribute2='value']
//input[ @type='email' and @class='form-control']....1 of 1

2.or
---------------
Syntax:
-----------
//tagname[@attribute1='value' or @attribute2='value']
//input[ @type='email' or @class='form-contro']....1 of 1

------------------------------------------------------------------
Xpath with Indexing/position()
============================
Syntax
==========
(xpath)[index]

OR

(xpath)[position()=index]

============================================================
Xpath Methods
=================
1.text()
---------------
- based on visible text of element we can identify element 
- text() never ignore white space

Syntax
===========
//tagname[text()='visible text']

2.normalize-space()
---------------------------
- based on visible text of element we can identify element 
- normalize-space() ignore white space like trim() of string class

Syntax
===========
//tagname[normalize-space()='visible text']

3.contains():Partial match
---------------------
Syntax:
==============
//tagname[contains(@attribute,'partial value')]

OR

//tagname[contains(text(),'partial text')]

//tagname[contains(normalize-space(),'partial text')]

Example:
---------------
//input[contains(@id,'searchtext')]


4.starts-with(): prefix value
-----------------------------------
Syntax:
==============
//tagname[starts-with(@attribute,'prefix value')]

OR

//tagname[starts-with(text(),'prefix text')]

//tagname[starts-with(normalize-space(),'prefix text')]

Example:
-------------
//input[starts-with(@id,'twotab')]
